---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Compare JPG, PNG and WebP Image Formats"
  description="Compare actual JPG, PNG, and WebP output sizes and previews in your browser. The original image stays on your device."
  noindex
  activeNav="/tools/"
>
  <section class="legal-hero legal-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL BROWSER TOOL</p>
    <h1>Compare formats using your own image.</h1>
    <p>
      Encode one unchanged image as JPG, PNG and WebP in this browser. Compare
      the byte counts and inspect the outputs before choosing a format for your
      listing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell comparison-panel page-section" data-format-compare>
    <div class="comparison-controls">
      <div>
        <label for="compare-file">Choose one product image</label>
        <input id="compare-file" type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp" />
        <p class="field-note">JPG, PNG or static WebP · up to 20 MB and 6 megapixels</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="compare-quality">JPG / WebP quality: <output id="compare-quality-value">85%</output></label>
        <input id="compare-quality" type="range" min="40" max="100" value="85" />
        <p class="field-note">PNG encoding does not use this quality setting.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="compare-background">Preview / JPG background</label>
        <input id="compare-background" type="color" value="#ffffff" />
        <p class="field-note">Transparent PNG/WebP previews use this background for comparison; their alpha channel is preserved.</p>
      </div>
      <button class="button" id="compare-run" type="button" disabled>Compare formats</button>
    </div>

    <p id="compare-status" class="status-line" role="status" aria-live="polite">
      Choose an image to begin. Your file is processed locally and is not uploaded.
    </p>

    <section id="compare-results" hidden aria-labelledby="compare-results-title">
      <h2 id="compare-results-title">Results from this browser</h2>
      <p id="compare-summary" class="field-note"></p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="format-results">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Requested format</th>
              <th scope="col">Actual output</th>
              <th scope="col">File size</th>
              <th scope="col">Change vs original</th>
              <th scope="col">Download</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="compare-rows"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div id="compare-previews" class="format-previews"></div>
    </section>
  </section>

  <section class="shell reading-section">
    <h2>How to make a fair comparison</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Use the same original file for all three encodings; this tool does not resize it.</li>
      <li>Compare the actual byte counts, then inspect fine texture, text and edges at normal size and at 100%.</li>
      <li>Try another image with different texture or transparency. One photo cannot predict every image.</li>
      <li>Confirm that the destination accepts the output type, then inspect its real listing preview.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Browser encoders can differ. If WebP is unsupported, the browser may
      return another format; the result table reports the actual MIME type and
      download extension instead of disguising it. For Etsy, see the
      <a href="/marketplace/etsy/">source-checked image reference</a> before
      uploading. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy explanation</a> and
      <a href="/methodology/">test limitations</a> for more detail.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import "../../scripts/format-compare";
</script>
